Grouping (design 2.3) and open/closed groups (design 2.4). Cells are named by their first word.

=== titles: Subtitle and Subsubtitle are plain members of the Title's group
--- before
#% title
# T
#% subtitle
# st
#% subsubtitle
# sst
#% text
# x
#% title
# T2
#% text
# y
--- groups
{T st sst x} {T2 y}

=== sections nest by level
--- before
#% text
# t0
#% section
# S
#% subsection
# SS
#% subsubsection
# SSS
#% text
# a
#% subsection
# SS2
#% text
# b
#% section
# S2
--- groups
t0 {S {SS {SSS a}} {SS2 b}} S2

=== inputs collect the outputs right after them
--- before
#% cell
i
#% output n=1
#= o
#% text
# t
#% cell
i2
#% output n=2
#| p
#? m
#= o2
#% output n=3
#= o3
#% cell
i3
#% cell
i4
#% output n=4
#= o4
--- groups
{i o} t {i2 p m o2 o3} i3 {i4 o4}

=== outputs after text are plain cells
--- before
#% code
c
#% output n=1
#= o
#% cell
i
#% text
# t
--- groups
{c o} i t

=== items collect items of higher level
--- before
#% item
# i
#% itemparagraph
# ip
#% subitem
# s
#% subsubitem
# ss
#% subitem
# s2
#% item
# i2
#% text
# t
#% itemnumbered
# n
#% subitemnumbered
# sn
--- groups
{i ip {s ss} s2} i2 t {n sn}

=== items collect input groups inside sections
--- before
#% section
# S
#% item
# i
#% subitem
# s
#% cell
c
#% output n=1
#= o
#% subsection
# SS
--- groups
{S {i {s {c o}}} SS}

=== a whole document
--- before
#% title
# Title
#% section
# S1
#% text
# t
#% cell
In
#% output n=1
#= Out
#% cell
x
#% subsection
# Sub
#% item
# i1
#% subitem
# s1
#% item
# i2
#% text
# t2
#% section
# S2
#% code
c
#% output n=2
#? m
#| pr
#= o
#% chapter
# cc
#% section
# sec
--- groups
{Title {S1 t {In Out} x {Sub {i1 s1} i2 t2}} {S2 {c m pr o}} {cc sec}}

=== a cell typed after a section's text joins the section
--- before
#% section
# S

#% text
# t
‖
--- keys
"x"
--- groups
{S t x}

=== double-clicking a group's bracket closes it showing its first cell, again opens it
--- before
#% section
# S

#% text
# t
--- keys
DoubleBracket(0,2)
--- after
#% section closed
# S

#% text
# t
‖

=== double-clicking a closed group's bracket opens it
--- before
#% section closed
# S

#% text
# t
--- keys
DoubleBracket(0,2)
--- after
#% section
# S

#% text
# t
‖

=== double-clicking a single cell's bracket does nothing
--- before
#% text
# t
--- keys
DoubleBracket(0,1)
--- after
#% text
# t
‖

=== Ctrl+' in an output closes the input group showing the output
--- before
#% cell label=1
print(1)
2
#% output n=2
#| 1
#= 2▮
--- keys
Ctrl+'
--- after
#% cell label=1 shown=3
print(1)
2
#% output n=2
#| 1
#= 2▮

=== Ctrl+' in the input closes the group showing the input; again opens it
--- before
#% cell label=1
2▮
#% output n=1
#= 2
--- keys
Ctrl+'
--- after
#% cell label=1 closed
2▮
#% output n=1
#= 2

=== Ctrl+' twice opens the group again
--- before
#% cell label=1
2▮
#% output n=1
#= 2
--- keys
Ctrl+' Ctrl+'
--- after
#% cell label=1
2▮
#% output n=1
#= 2

=== Ctrl+A then Ctrl+} closes every group, nested ones too; Ctrl+{ opens them
--- before
#% section
# S
#% subsection
# SS
#% text
# a
#% cell
x
#% output n=1
#= 1
‖
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+}
--- after
#% section closed ◆
# S

#% subsection closed ◆
# SS

#% text ◆
# a

#% cell closed ◆
x
#% output n=1
#= 1 ◆

=== Ctrl+{ opens every group of the selection
--- before
#% section closed
# S
#% subsection closed
# SS
#% text
# a
--- keys
Ctrl+A Ctrl+{
--- after
#% section ◆
# S

#% subsection ◆
# SS

#% text ◆
# a

=== a cell typed after a closed group's head lands in the group and opens it
--- before
#% section closed
# S

#% text
# t
‖
--- keys
"x"
--- after
#% section
# S

#% text
# t

#% cell
x▮
--- groups
{S t x}

=== Down skips the cells hidden in a closed group, keeping the column
--- before
#% section closed
# S▮

#% text
# hidden

#% section
# S2
--- keys
Down Down
--- after
#% section closed
# S

#% text
# hidden

#% section
# S▮2

=== cells grouped by hand
--- before
#% text
# a

#% text
# b

#% text
# c
--- keys
Bracket(0) Shift+Bracket(1) Ctrl+Shift+G
--- after
#% text together ◆
# a

#% text together ◆
# b

#% text
# c
--- groups
{a b} c

=== ungrouping removes the marks of the whole run
--- before
#% text together
# a▮

#% text together
# b

#% text
# c
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+U
--- groups
a b c

=== manual grouping keeps only groups by hand
--- before
#! mathcas 2 notebook grouping=manual

#% section
# S

#% text together
# a

#% text together
# b
--- groups
S {a b}
